From 8586236549227528af17cb0e4cac5d7d63af4239 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mauri <mauricio@heyglide.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 14:23:10 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] GLES 3.0 / WebGL2 renderer: 3D layer into a 496x384
 framebuffer object

model2_geo_gl.c drawn through the subset OpenGL ES 3.0 / WebGL2 and the
desktop 2.1 compatibility context share: GLSL ES 3.00 or GLSL 1.20 shaders
(a mat4 uniform for the projection instead of ftransform), one vertex
buffer with each triangle's material in its vertices and one glDrawArrays
per phase, R8 (ES) / LUMINANCE (desktop) index sheets, an RGBA8 atlas of
the palette LUTs, no fixed-function matrices, client arrays or immediate
mode. The 3D layer is rendered into its own 496x384 framebuffer (RGBA8 +
depth24/stencil8; the stencil is the fillmap) and composited over the
caller's framebuffer, so the picture does not depend on the window.

New entry points for a caller that composites itself:
model2_geo_gl_projection_matrix, _set_mvp, _set_target_size,
_render_offscreen, _target_texture, _composite_target, _set_lut_per_frame.
model2_gl.h: <GLES3/gl3.h> under Emscripten (MODEL2_GL_ES), the Windows
loader extended to the new entry points, model2_gl_have_sync().
